# Batch read (64 blocks) throughput (Kelem/s) by I/O strategy.
# SOURCE: docs/io_uring_migration/benchmark_results.md
#   "Phase 6: Real-disk re-run on AMD Threadripper PRO 5975WX (2026-07-10)" ->
#   "Batch read (cmp_batch_read, 64 x 256 KB blocks)" table (Throughput row):
#   mmap sequential 87.2, io_uring batch SQE 13.0, io_uring sequential 4.9
#   (Kelem/s). On real disk mmap's cache-served batch leads 6.7x; io_uring's
#   SQE batching still beats its own sequential path 2.65x. 256 KB blocks,
#   Samsung 990 PRO NVMe, ext4 /dev/nvme0n1p4 (real O_DIRECT), 2026-07-10.
# Re-run on current hardware; supersedes the 2026-02-20 Phase 3 figure.
# NOTE: label underscores are enhanced-text-escaped (\\_) so gnuplot renders a
# literal "_" rather than a subscript; \n stays a single backslash (newline).
#
# index  strategy_label              throughput_kelems  color_id
0   "mmap\n(sequential)"            87.2   1
1   "io\\_uring\n(batch SQE)"       13.0   2
2   "io\\_uring\n(sequential)"      4.9    3
